drm/amdgpu: keep the HDP flush remap in the 4 KiB register hole

The NBIO/NBIF blocks remap HDP_MEM_FLUSH_CNTL and HDP_REG_FLUSH_CNTL into
an unused 4 KiB page at the end of the first 512 KiB of the register BAR
(KFD_MMIO_REMAP_HDP_MEM_FLUSH_CNTL and _REG_FLUSH_CNTL are offsets 0 and 4
in it), so a process can flush HDP after storing into VRAM through the BAR.
The hole is a property of the hardware, but MMIO_REG_HOLE_OFFSET was
written as 0x80000 - PAGE_SIZE: on a kernel with larger pages it moved into
live registers, so the remap was turned off there (CVE-2024-41011), and the
flush went back to the NBIF register with nothing for user space.

The MacLinuxGPU driver runs this code with 16 KiB pages (the host's) and
hands a KFD client the HDP flush page itself (dext/sources/hdp_flush.h). The
hole now stays at 0x80000 - AMDGPU_GPU_PAGE_SIZE, the 4 KiB page the
hardware leaves unused, whatever the page size, and the remap is programmed
for every non-SR-IOV device as on a 4 KiB kernel. KFD's MMIO_REMAP
allocation, its MMIO mmap and the MMIO_REMAP TTM BO keep refusing pages
larger than 4 KiB, so nothing upstream maps the page into a process; the
driver maps it itself after checking that no register block of the device
starts in the rest of the host page (rt_kfd_session_hdp_flush). With 4 KiB
pages nothing changes.

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/nbif_v6_3_1.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/nbif_v6_3_1.c
index b6f832c..951710f 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/nbif_v6_3_1.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/nbif_v6_3_1.c
@@ -493,11 +493,11 @@ static void nbif_v6_3_1_program_aspm(struct amdgpu_device *adev)
 #endif
 }
 
-#define MMIO_REG_HOLE_OFFSET (0x80000 - PAGE_SIZE)
+#define MMIO_REG_HOLE_OFFSET (0x80000 - AMDGPU_GPU_PAGE_SIZE)
 
 static void nbif_v6_3_1_set_reg_remap(struct amdgpu_device *adev)
 {
-	if (!amdgpu_sriov_vf(adev) && (PAGE_SIZE <= 4096)) {
+	if (!amdgpu_sriov_vf(adev)) {
 		adev->rmmio_remap.reg_offset = MMIO_REG_HOLE_OFFSET;
 		adev->rmmio_remap.bus_addr = adev->rmmio_base + MMIO_REG_HOLE_OFFSET;
 	} else {
